{"step_index":593,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:38:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T06:38:35+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T06:38:36+08:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n--- ALL P TAGS IN QUIZ06 ---\n<p>20 items &bull; 20 seconds per question &bull; Do not switch tabs or windows.</p>\n<p id=\"err\" style=\"color:var(--bad);margin:0 0 10px\"></p>\n<p id=\"lk1\">You can no longer open or retake this quiz.</p>\n<p id=\"lk2\"></p>\n<p id=\"rd\"></p>\n<p style=\"font-size:.85rem\">Give the downloaded file or the result code to your instructor. Your result is also saved on this device.</p>\n<p><b>-1 point</b> will be deducted from your score.<br>Total violations: <b id=\"wc\">0</b></p>\n--- ALL LI TAGS IN QUIZ06 ---\n<li>Each question has <b>20 seconds</b>. When time runs out, it moves on automatically with no points.</li>\n<li>Every alt-tab or switch to another tab/app costs <b>-1 point</b>.</li>\n<li>You cannot go back to previous questions.</li>\n<li>Your score and per-question feedback appear right after the quiz.</li>\n"}
{"step_index":594,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:38:36Z","input_tokens":3378,"cache_read_tokens":125479,"output_tokens":974,"thinking":"The instruction to provide the downloaded file or result code to the instructor is found exclusively within the HTML file associated with the specific quiz (QUIZ06). This suggests the expected user action involves downloading a result file and then providing it to the instructor, or providing a result code. A download button is present in the main index file, as well.\n\n\nThe initial focus was on modifying the student-facing quiz interface based on auto-submission settings. The intent shifted to implementing auto-recording functionality in the teacher interface (`teacher.html`). This involves updating the settings state, connecting a button to the auto-record setting, and ensuring the setting is saved to persistent storage.\n\n\nIf auto-recording is enabled, the result screen instructions must be updated to reflect automatic submission. Conversely, if auto-recording is disabled, the instructions should remain unchanged, referencing the download file or result code requirement. Confirmed that the start screen instructions do not require modification.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"student quiz submission confirmation ux copy feedback text web"}}]}
{"step_index":595,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:38:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T06:38:45+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T06:38:49+08:00\nThe search for \"student quiz submission confirmation ux copy feedback text web\" returned the following summary:\nDesigning the UX copy and feedback text for a **student quiz submission confirmation** requires a delicate balance. Students are often anxious about whether their work went through, if their answers saved correctly, and when they will see a grade. \n\nDepending on your product’s architecture and grading policy, here is a breakdown of UX copy best practices, structure patterns, and ready-to-use examples for web applications.\n\n---\n\n### Key Elements of a Great Quiz Submission State\n1. **Immediate Reassurance:** Address the primary user anxiety right away (*\"Did it actually submit?\"*). Use a clear visual indicator like a green checkmark alongside the text[1].\n2. **Set Clear Expectations:** Tell the student what happens next (e.g., *Are scores visible immediately? Will the instructor review it manually?*)[2][1].\n3. **Provide a Safe Exit:** Give a clear path forward, such as returning to the course dashboard or viewing results (if permitted)[3].\n\n---\n\n### UX Copy Options by Scenario\n\n#### Scenario A: Automated Grading (Instant Score Available)\n*Best for multiple-choice or auto-graded quizzes where students can see results right away.*\n\n* **Header/Title:** Quiz submitted\n* **Body Text:** You answered 8 out of 10 questions correctly. Your score has been saved to your gradebook.\n* **Primary CTA:** [View detailed results]\n* **Secondary CTA:** [Return to course]\n\n#### Scenario B: Manual Instructor Grading (No Instant Score)\n*Best for essay-heavy quizzes, open-ended questions, or instances where scores are hidden until a deadline passes[2][4].*\n\n* **Header/Title:** Quiz submitted successfully\n* **Body Text:** Your professor will review your answers[2]. You’ll receive a notification when your grade is posted.\n* **Primary CTA:** [Return to dashboard]\n\n#### Scenario C: Timed/High-Stakes Exams (Strict Closure)\n*Best for midterms or finals where students cannot retake or re-enter the quiz view.*\n\n* **Header/Title:** Exam officially submitted\n* **Body Text:** Submitted on Oct 24, 2026 at 2:15 PM. This attempt is locked and cannot be edited.\n* **Primary CTA:** [Back to assignments]\n\n---\n\n### Before & After: Refining the Microcopy\n\n| Approach | Weak Copy (Vague / Robotic) | Optimized UX Copy (Clear / Reassuring) | Why it’s better |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Too technical** | `Error Code 0: Transaction committed via DB sync. Session closed.` | `Quiz submitted successfully. You're all set!` | Eliminates jargon; uses human-friendly, plain language. |\n| **Too brief** | `Success.` | `Quiz submitted. We've saved your answers.` | Confirms *what* was successfully completed so the user isn't left guessing[3][1]. |\n| **Anxiety-inducing** | `Warning: You can no longer change your answers. Proceed?` | `Quiz submitted! Your responses are locked and safely stored.` | Replaces a threatening warning tone with a reassuring confirmation[5]. |\n\n---\n\n### UX Writing Guidelines for this Flow\n\n* **Avoid Over-Celebration:** Unless it’s a gamified learning module, avoid words like *\"Amazing!\"* or *\"Woohoo!\"* for routine academic quiz submissions[3][1]. Keep the tone encouraging, calm, and professional.\n* **Avoid \"Success!\" as a standalone title:** Instead, name the exact action that succeeded (e.g., *\"Quiz submitted\"* or *\"Assignment received\"*)[3][1]. \n* **Timestamp the submission:** If technical glitches are a common concern on your platform, displaying a precise timestamp (*\"Submitted today at 3:14 PM\"*) drastically reduces student support tickets.\n\nSources:\n[1] [mintlify.app](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH4VzJpSzsX5Gb_JdJ3apLRhRh6lx2ULYo8k_HvlvSTUhfNhcsz0SF_qIL9DeGBFJhIqiPlyKXR0iJPX-cnaBrUaXf3Y92RYKM6bYZN1vJOAlVZiRu6AXwyiUS8AT9XSIIxAlPhSq9r8zm1UwOhkPuAzgkF9qZUvCCH2JTFlQKvZ26ktfKF3n8=)\n[2] [instructure.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE8C4l2Ql5U-JzTDeGNQwND1QNsW8hC_D5ncVVIQEOC1Ytgr6BJPWXfPWdhyJZuTuY0wmfizZV_V9rPiCzMgHWpHYPNpWivGJlQDBqfOZxJ6lQNtvHoSDAEu2jNhM29T0m1K_mtneWCA6sJmexDPQptavOL0UmoPpa43HNnbo60hFAdXW8ka2AhH7D7xNrddJntFrde_HMW7QlPts3_vv5y_o82To7O-I6-Ux7LNJDbI2MUTe7n)\n[3] [atlassian.design](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlYP0u3vvg6coaCZHNcJ0DLZEdDcU4lz3FUQOaAx_Vdp-sYPBYUYT4_ubh9DWQ_OVCNEF3xkhdQk_HdXoKDtX-dBbT2TfkscAVzWxAGBx1PphJEyhr8hGjtSmAodG9xQxxdGmhITDl0aCdhJpaD9ppaAVsUXTSK6fNseQAIC2kxC-Oy_YE-Q==)\n[4] [edublogs.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHRv78wyofxqZmRvFfvTqz4WVKsfz-0Mvmcbb4_POzq7JZTyUpj4cdrUIQ8f7U0xjrmL1GvPmwjDqedFvkkC8oIYKC8J6cOF3GXtdpLs-fD9nwlBwhyknI7StaaVTQP4D19S2OSEsxkRrGXRIgYq56aWQnFDSoruyHtPLUQsFYNhFX10xxdrARF2g==)\n[5] [pencilandpaper.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGRPlQYvj_UQHvzdpOQFtGBaHFtr6kNc9O488nglqMsF4BIQ_fL6frnXeq8PIcieKK1NAAHv0ZR9bD5HoumhunFUIOh3H-QpG8oS_A2v5iKYym3OCjTgPJlk60XzNMzJ4-s5tH6E__j)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":596,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:38:50Z","input_tokens":2726,"cache_read_tokens":128868,"output_tokens":2084,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: when the \"Auto Record Quiz\" feature is enabled, the interface needs adjustments to reflect automatic submission. Specifically, download and copy options should be hidden, and the instruction text updated.\nThe primary HTML file (`index.html`) requires modification.\nThe elements with IDs `#dl` (download container) and `#cp` (copy container) must be hidden. The instruction note displayed below the score needs to be revised to reflect the automatic submission rather than manual download/copy actions.\n\n\nThe interface adjustments involve hiding download/copy UI elements and updating the instruction text in `index.html`. Also, `<button id=\"lkdl\">Download Result File</button>` needs to be hidden when re-opening a completed quiz on `#lock`. In `teacher.html`, the auto-record button (`#btn-auto-rec`) should bind to `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` and persist the setting to Firestore. This requires detailed verification of the changes. The changes are non-major; thus, the update needs to be documented in `HISTORY.md`, following the specified format. The `implementation_plan.md` artifact will be used for planning.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan to conditionally hide result download and copy buttons and update instruction copy when auto submission is active.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Auto Submission Mode - Hide Result File/Code & Update Instructions\n\n## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\n\n1. **Conditional Result Action Display in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)**:\n   - When `autoRecordQuiz` is active (`settings.autoRecordQuiz !== false`):\n     - Hide the download and copy buttons (`#dl` \"Download Result File\" and `#cp` \"Copy Result Code\").\n     - Update the result card's instructions paragraph from:\n       `\"Give the downloaded file or the result code to your instructor. Your result is also saved on this device.\"`\n       to:\n       `\"Your response has been automatically submitted to your instructor. Your result is also saved on this device.\"`\n     - On the lock screen (`#lock`), hide `#lkdl` (\"Download Result File\").\n   - When `autoRecordQuiz === false`:\n     - Keep the buttons visible and retain the original manual file/code submission instruction.\n\n2. **Connect Setting in [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)**:\n   - Wire `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` to the existing `#btn-auto-rec` toggle (default `true`).\n   - Persist `autoRecordQuiz` in the Firestore settings payload on \"Save to Quiz\".\n   - Sync `syncOptionsUI()` to reflect the loaded `autoRecordQuiz` state from Firestore.\n\n3. **Re-sync Firestore Template**:\n   - Synchronize `quizzes/template` in Firestore so downloaded quiz files contain the updated conditional logic.\n\n---\n\n## 2. File Modifications\n\n### 2.1 [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)\n- In `settingsState`:\n  Add `autoRecordQuiz: true`.\n- In `syncOptionsUI()`:\n  Update `#btn-auto-rec` to use `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`.\n- In `btn-auto-rec.onclick`:\n  Toggle `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz = !settingsState.autoRecordQuiz; syncOptionsUI();`.\n- In `save-btn.onclick`:\n  `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` is saved as part of `settingsState` into Firestore `quizzes/{quizId}`.\n\n### 2.2 [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)\n- In HTML markup:\n  Wrap `#dl` and `#cp` buttons in `<div id=\"res-actions\" class=\"row\" style=\"justify-content:center\">...</div>`.\n  Give the instructions paragraph an ID: `<p id=\"res-note\" style=\"font-size:.85rem\">...</p>`.\n- In `show()` or `initDisplay()` / quiz end:\n  - If `settings.autoRecordQuiz !== false`:\n    - `$('res-actions').style.display = 'none';`\n    - `$('res-note').textContent = 'Your response has been automatically submitted to your instructor. Your result is also saved on this device.';`\n    - On `#lock`, ensure `$('lkdl').classList.add('hide');`.\n  - Else:\n    - `$('res-actions').style.display = 'flex';`\n    - `$('res-note').textContent = 'Give the downloaded file or the result code to your instructor. Your result is also saved on this device.';`\n\n### 2.3 [HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md)\n- Append Non-Major Patch 1.0.14 documenting the functional wiring of `autoRecordQuiz`, conditional hiding of result actions, and updated student instructions per Rule 1.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency & Ripple Effect Analysis\n\n| Component / Flow | Dependency Type | Potential Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Result Card (`#res`) | Direct UI | Layout shift when buttons hide | Wrapped buttons in `#res-actions` container; toggled container display; instruction text remains in identical position. |\n| Lock Screen (`#lock`) | Direct UI | Inadvertent file download exposure on lock | Explicitly check `autoRecordQuiz` before showing `#lkdl`. |\n| Teacher Save Payload | Data contract | Firestore schema rejection | Security rule for `quizzes/{quizId}` is `allow read, write: if true;`, accepting `autoRecordQuiz` boolean without schema errors. |\n| Student Submission | Database write | Blocked submission | `saveSubmission` already auto-posts to `quizzes/{quizId}/submissions` upon quiz completion; hiding buttons purely removes redundant manual handoff steps. |\n| Original File | Untouchable asset | Rule violation | `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` kept untouched per Rules 2 & 12. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification Plan (Rules 3 & 10)\n\n1. **Auto Record ON Mode Verification**:\n   - Test quiz completion with `autoRecordQuiz: true`:\n     - Verify `#res-actions` is hidden.\n     - Verify `#res-note` displays *\"Your response has been automatically submitted to your instructor. Your result is also saved on this device.\"*.\n     - Verify submission document is posted to Firestore.\n2. **Auto Record OFF Mode Verification**:\n   - Test quiz completion with `autoRecordQuiz: false`:\n     - Verify `#res-actions` is visible with both buttons.\n     - Verify `#res-note` displays original manual handoff text.\n3. **Teacher Portal Setting Persistence**:\n   - Verify toggling `#btn-auto-rec` in `teacher.html` and clicking \"Save to Quiz\" updates Firestore `quizzes/active` with `autoRecordQuiz: true/false`.\n4. **Rule 9 Zero-Comment Compliance**:\n   - Verify 0 comments or docstrings across all modified files.\n5. **Original File Integrity**:\n   - Confirm `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` remains completely untouched.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
